# Ledgers are append-only records: a merge that picks a side deletes content (Crucible FB-13, three times).
# union keeps both sides; the one thing it cannot do is dedupe a stateful single line (## Now:, a ledger row),
# which is why `adu ledger lint` checks for duplicates after every merge and fails toward noise, never silence.
STATUS.md merge=union
SESSION-JOURNAL.md merge=union
OPEN-QUESTIONS.md merge=union
FEEDBACK.md merge=union
RETRO.md merge=union
VERSIONS.md merge=union
DECISIONS.md merge=union
# Fixtures and lock files keep LF on every platform (Crucible FB-20: CRLF fixtures failed on Windows clones).
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
